{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":60933,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040e6ae5815b0a7a9a34ac17529516e1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 12 screens built. Now wire prototype interactions:\n\n1. 01_Splash → 02_Onboarding: auto (after delay). On the frame itself: reactions on frame.\n2. 02_Onboarding Get Started button → 03_Sign_In.\n3. 03_Sign_In phone number field → 04_Verification (tap on the phone input area). \n4. 04_Verification: back → 03_Sign_In; next → 05_Home.\n5. 05_Home: Red Apple card → 06_Product_Detail; tabs → 05/07/09/12.\n6. 06_Product_Detail: back → 05_Home; Add To Basket → 09_My_Cart.\n7. 07_Explore: Beverages tile → 08_Beverages; tabs → 05/07/09/12.\n8. 08_Beverages: back → 07_Explore.\n9. 09_My_Cart: Go to Checkout → 10_Checkout_Overlay (overlay open); tabs.\n10. 10_Checkout_Overlay: close → 09_My_Cart (overlay close / swap back); Place Order → 11_Order_Accepted.\n11. 11_Order_Accepted: Back to home → 05_Home.\n12. 12_Account: tabs.\n\nFor nav tab interactions inside a component set variant instance — each variant instance has its own children; adding reactions to the shared component children would propagate to all variants. But the current-tab differs. If I add reactions on tab label/icon nodes in the components, they'll be identical across all variants — good: Shop→05_Home, Explore→07_Explore, Cart→09_My_Cart, Account→12_Account. Favourite entry-only, no link needed. I can add reactions inside one variant's children... but component variants are separate components; adding to each of 4 variants would be 16 reactions. Alternatively add to component children before combineAsVariants — too late, they're already combined. I'll add reactions to each variant's tab label/icon nodes.\n\nActually instances of variants — the nodes inside instances inherit from component; reactions added on component children propagate to instances. I need to add the reactions once per variant component (4 variants). Let me do that.\n\nFor the checkout overlay: use reaction with action type \"OVERLAY\" opening 10 frame? Actually 10_Checkout_Overlay is a full frame that includes the cart behind. Simplest: Go to Checkout → navigate to 10_Checkout_Overlay frame. Brief says \"opens over 09_My_Cart; the cart stays behind it\" — the design shows it. For prototype, \"Open overlay\" action pointing to the sheet... but the sheet is inside frame 10. Easier: On tap Go to Checkout → open overlay → destination: 10_Checkout_Overlay frame (as overlay centered? No — it's a full screen frame; opening as overlay would offset it). Alternative: simple \"Navigate to\" 10_Checkout_Overlay. Visually it shows the cart behind with scrim and sheet, satisfying the requirement. The evaluators check flow & prototype completeness. I'll use Navigate to for simplicity and reliability. Hmm, but brief explicitly says \"10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09_My_Cart\" — using overlay action would be more faithful. However, opening the full 414×896 frame as overlay requires a position; \"Manual\" position can't easily be set via reactions API? The Plugin API reaction action: {type:\"OVERLAY\", navigation:\"OVERLAY\", destinationId, overlayPosition:\"CENTER\", overlayRelativePosition:null}. Position CENTER would center it over cart — full-screen frame centered = covers everything, looks same as navigate. That works: overlay covers cart frame, scrim is included. Let me use OVERLAY with position CENTER. Close → \"CLOSE\" action navigation \"CLOSE_OVERLAY\"? Action type \"CLOSE\" with navigation \"CLOSE_OVERLAY\". In Plugin API: actions include {type:\"CLOSE\", navigation:\"CLOSE_OVERLAY\"} I believe... Actually the Action union: navigation: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"CLOSE_OVERLAY\" | \"SWAP\" | \"SCROLL_TO\" | \"CHANGE_TO\" | \"BACK\". For close overlay: {type:\"CLOSE\", navigation:\"CLOSE_OVERLAY\"}? Hmm, let me recall: Action = { type: \"BACK\"|\"CLOSE\"|\"URL\"|\"UPDATE_VARIANT\"|\"SET_VARIABLE\"|... ; navigation?...} Actually the documented shape: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", ...}. For close: {type:\"CLOSE\", navigation:\"CLOSE_OVERLAY\"}? I've seen examples: reactions: [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions:[{type:\"CLOSE\", navigation:\"CLOSE_OVERLAY\"}]}]? Not 100% sure. Safer: close button → Navigate to 09_My_Cart. That still satisfies \"close → 09_My_Cart\" link. I'll use navigate for both to be safe, except maybe use overlay open for checkout since it's in the brief. Let me try OVERLAY; if API errors, fall back to NAVIGATE.\n\nAuto transition 01→02: trigger {type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 1500}? The Trigger type for delayed: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\" with timeout in ms (device? it's \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\": {type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 800}). Yes.\n\nReaction structure in Plugin API: node.reactions = [{trigger: {type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions: [{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"...\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:null, preserveScrollPosition:false}]}]. \n\nTransition: {type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\", easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\"}, duration:0.3} or null for instant.\n\nLet me now find the nodes to attach reactions:\n- 01_Splash frame itself: AFTER_TIMEOUT → 02.\n- 02_Onboarding: the button instance.\n- 03_Sign_In: phone input — attach to the \"placeholder-number\" text? Better to the underline area... attach to the whole phone row. Simplest: attach to placeholder text node and code text. I'll attach to \"placeholder-number\" text node. Maybe also create an invisible hotspot rectangle over the phone field. I'll attach to the placeholder text.\n- 04_Verification: back instance (9:2 instance), next ellipse.\n- 05_Home: Red Apple card instance (the one with name \"Red Apple\"); NavBar instance children tabs. NavBar reactions must be added on component variants so all instances inherit. But wait — nav instances on screens: 05 uses Shop variant etc. Add reactions per variant: in each variant component, find icon+label for Shop/Explore/Cart/Account and add navigate reactions. That gives all instances links. \n\nBut caution: component reactions on variant children propagate to instances — yes.\n\n- 06: back → 05, addBtn → 09.\n- 07: Beverages tile (6th tile) → 08.\n- 08: back → 07.\n- 09: cb button → overlay open 10.\n- 10: close instance → navigate 09 (or close overlay); Place Order → 11.\n- 11: back-home text → 05.\n- 12: nav tabs already from variants.\n\nOverlay open from a button inside 09 with destination full frame — position \"CENTER\". The overlay frame has fixed position; when opened as overlay centered on the cart screen, it covers it exactly (same size). Good.\n\nClose: I'll use NAVIGATE back to 09 to be safe.\n\nAlso add reactions for the tab labels inside variants: need to load fonts? Setting reactions doesn't need fonts.\n\nLet me write the prototype wiring code.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06ae3923-d12a-4248-9468-ebfe96d71820","uuid":"ce087307-6535-4376-9b05-b8cecc960edc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:49:54.554Z","thinking_duration_ms":34473}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":60933,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040e6ae5815b0a7a9a34ac17529516e1","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_24_f3eb523b","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"7:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nconst byName = n => ws.findOne(x=>x.name===n);\nconst F = {}; for (const nm of [\"01_Splash\",\"02_Onboarding\",\"03_Sign_In\",\"04_Verification\",\"05_Home\",\"06_Product_Detail\",\"07_Explore\",\"08_Beverages\",\"09_My_Cart\",\"10_Checkout_Overlay\",\"11_Order_Accepted\",\"12_Account\"]) F[nm]=byName(nm);\nfunction nav(dest){ return {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:dest.id, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\",easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\"},duration:0.3}, preserveScrollPosition:false}; }\nfunction navInstant(dest){ return {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:dest.id, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:null, preserveScrollPosition:false}; }\nfunction overlay(dest){ return {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:dest.id, navigation:\"OVERLAY\", overlayPosition:\"CENTER\", transition:{type:\"MOVE_IN\",easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"},duration:0.3}, preserveScrollPosition:false}; }\nfunction click(node, action){ node.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions:[action]}]; }\n\n// 01 -> 02 auto\nF[\"01_Splash\"].reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\",timeout:1500}, actions:[nav(F[\"02_Onboarding\"])]}];\n// 02 Get Started -> 03\nclick(F[\"02_Onboarding\"].findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Button\"), nav(F[\"03_Sign_In\"]));\n// 03 phone field -> 04 (hotspot over phone input)\nconst s3=F[\"03_Sign_In\"];\nconst hot=figma.createRectangle(); hot.name=\"phone-hotspot\"; hot.x=24; hot.y=456; hot.resize(366,62); hot.fills=[]; s3.appendChild(hot);\nclick(hot, nav(F[\"04_Verification\"]));\n// 04 back -> 03, next -> 05\nconst s4=F[\"04_Verification\"];\nclick(s4.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"IconButton/Back\"), nav(F[\"03_Sign_In\"]));\nclick(s4.findOne(n=>n.name===\"next\"), nav(F[\"05_Home\"]));\n// 05 Red Apple -> 06\nconst s5=F[\"05_Home\"];\nconst appleCard=s5.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"ProductCard\").find(c=>{const t=c.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\"&&n.name===\"name\");return t&&t.characters===\"Red Apple\";});\nclick(appleCard, nav(F[\"06_Product_Detail\"]));\n// 06 back -> 05, Add To Basket -> 09\nconst s6=F[\"06_Product_Detail\"];\nclick(s6.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"IconButton/Back\"), nav(F[\"05_Home\"]));\nclick(s6.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Button\"), nav(F[\"09_My_Cart\"]));\n// 07 Beverages tile -> 08\nconst s7=F[\"07_Explore\"];\nconst bevTile=s7.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"CategoryTile\").find(c=>{const t=c.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\"&&n.name===\"label\");return t&&t.characters===\"Beverages\";});\nclick(bevTile, nav(F[\"08_Beverages\"]));\n// 08 back -> 07\nconst s8=F[\"08_Beverages\"];\nclick(s8.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"IconButton/Back\"), nav(F[\"07_Explore\"]));\n// 09 Go to Checkout -> overlay 10\nconst s9=F[\"09_My_Cart\"];\nclick(s9.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Button\"), overlay(F[\"10_Checkout_Overlay\"]));\n// 10 close -> 09, Place Order -> 11\nconst s10=F[\"10_Checkout_Overlay\"];\nclick(s10.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"IconButton/Close\"), navInstant(F[\"09_My_Cart\"]));\nclick(s10.findOne(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Button\"), nav(F[\"11_Order_Accepted\"]));\n// 11 Back to home -> 05\nclick(F[\"11_Order_Accepted\"].findOne(n=>n.name===\"back-home\"), nav(F[\"05_Home\"]));\n\n// NavBar variant tab links\nconst navSet=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"10:193\");\nconst tabDest={Shop:\"05_Home\",Explore:\"07_Explore\",Cart:\"09_My_Cart\",Account:\"12_Account\"};\nlet count=0;\nfor(const variant of navSet.children){\n  for(const tab of [\"Shop\",\"Explore\",\"Cart\",\"Account\"]){\n    const label=variant.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\"&&n.name===\"label-\"+tab);\n    if(label){ click(label, navInstant(F[tabDest[tab]])); count++; }\n  }\n}\nreturn \"prototype wired, nav links: \"+count;","description":"Wire all prototype interactions across the 12 frames and NavBar variants","fileKey":"rOzSn1MkRakcwc5zqsVINX"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06ae3923-d12a-4248-9468-ebfe96d71820","uuid":"e4791519-1be9-4b40-8e88-58c272a1027f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:50:11.352Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_24_f3eb523b","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
