{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":63777,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040e6ae581970a7ac5d6b6aeba16554e","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Action format is wrong. Correct format for navigate action in reactions:\n```\n{type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: {...}}\n```\nThe error suggests 'NODE' isn't valid for type; expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE'... Hmm, the API for reactions: action types include \"BACK\", \"CLOSE\", \"URL\", \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\", \"SET_VARIABLE\", \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\", \"CONDITIONAL\", and navigation actions use `type: \"NODE\"`? Let me recall. In Figma Plugin API, Reaction = { trigger, actions: Action[] }. Action for navigation is:\n```\n{\n  type: \"NODE\",\n  destinationId: string | null,\n  navigation: Navigation,\n  transition: Transition | null,\n  preserveScrollPosition: boolean,\n  overlayRelativePosition?: Vector,\n  overlayBackground?: ...\n}\n```\nThat should be valid... The error at [0].actions[0] shows my OVERLAY action failed (MOVE_IN not allowed transition for that?). Wait — the error trace says `at click ... PLUGIN line 39`. Line 39 in my code corresponds to which click? The error message's transition complaint: \"Expected [0].actions[0].transition ... received 'MOVE_IN'\" — so it's the overlay() action that failed. But that was the 4th click... Actually maybe some clicks partially applied. The one failing has transition MOVE_IN — only overlay uses MOVE_IN. So clicks 1-4 (before 09) succeeded, and the overlay click failed.\n\nFor OVERLAY navigation, correct action shape:\n```\n{\n  type: \"NODE\",\n  destinationId,\n  navigation: \"OVERLAY\",\n  transition: {type:\"MOVE_IN\", direction:\"BOTTOM\", duration, easing, matchLayers?...} — hmm\n}\n```\nActually in Plugin API, Transition type for OVERLAY: `EasingDirectionTransition` includes direction & matchLayers for MOVE_IN/SLIDE_IN/PUSH. The error shows one candidate expected `direction` and `matchLayers` (that's the SMART/SCROLL variant?) and \"Expected null, received object at transition\" — one branch expects transition:null. For OVERLAY navigation, maybe transition must be null? No — overlays can have MOVE_IN transitions. The listed candidate: 'DISSOLVE'|'SMART_ANIMATE'|'SCROLL_ANIMATE' (that's `transition` without direction), another requires direction+matchLayers. Hmm, direction/matchLayers required — so for MOVE_IN include direction:\"BOTTOM\" and matchLayers:false. But wait the error was raised for the OVERLAY action — actually re-reading: the failed action had navigation:\"OVERLAY\", overlayPosition — \"Unrecognized key(s): 'overlayPosition'\". So the key isn't overlayPosition. Correct keys for overlay action: `overlayPosition` isn't a thing; it's `overlayRelativePosition` (a Vector) plus `overlayBackgroundType` (\"NONE\"|\"AUTO\"|\"MANUAL\") and `overlayBackgroundInteraction`? Let me recall from docs:\n\n```\ninterface NavigateToAction {\n  type: \"NODE\"\n  navigation: Navigation // \"NAVIGATE\" | \"OVERLAY\" | ...\n  destinationId: string | null\n  transition: Transition | null\n  preserveScrollPosition: boolean\n  overlayRelativePosition?: Vector\n  overlayBackground?: \"NONE\" | \"AUTO\" | \"MANUAL\"  // hmm\n}\n```\n\nTo be safe, simplest: for overlay use navigation:\"OVERLAY\", transition:null, preserveScrollPosition:false, overlayRelativePosition:{x:0,y:0}. If overlayPosition unknown keys cause failure, omit. Also for swap/back: navigation \"BACK\".\n\nAlso verify clicks before failed one applied — clicks 1..4 (02→03, hotspot 03→04, 04 back→03, next→05, 05 apple→06, 06 back→05, 06 button→09, 07 bev→08, 08 back→07, 09 checkout→overlay FAILED). Since error stopped execution, the remaining ones (10, 11, navbar) not applied.\n\nRetry with corrected action formats.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06ae3923-d12a-4248-9468-ebfe96d71820","uuid":"856af856-8868-4260-b712-d8016a87565f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:50:37.936Z","thinking_duration_ms":19135}
